# Generated host-app shell. Materialized by `bootstrap.sh`, which runs
# `npx @react-native-community/cli init` and then patches the generated
# files. Committing the generated app would balloon the repo with hundreds
# of files (Xcode project blobs, gradle wrappers) that contribute nothing
# beyond what the bootstrap script can recreate from the upstream RN template.
#
# Files we DO keep in git: App.tsx, index.js, app.json, package.json,
# {babel,metro,tsconfig}.* — everything that's actually about *this* app
# rather than the RN template.
node_modules/
ios/
android/
.host/
*.log
yarn.lock
package-lock.json
